 "answer": "In the context of the LlamaIndex project documents provided, there are a couple of examples where an index is saved to disk. Let's focus on the relevant parts:\n\n1. **Improvement #1 - Create a Starting Index** in the document titled \"Putting it All Together\" (context reference [2]):\n\n   - The code snippet shows a function `insert_terms` where, after inserting terms into the `llama_index`, the index is saved to disk using the method `st.session_state[\"llama_index\"].storage_context.persist()`.\n   - Although the specific directory name isn't explicitly mentioned in the snippet provided, it's implied that the default directory used by `persist()` is `./storage` based on the default behavior described in the document titled \"Persisting & Loading Data\" (context reference [5]).\n\n2. **Persisting to disk** in the document titled \"Storing\" (context reference [7]):\n\n   - The method `index.storage_context.persist(persist_dir=\"<persist_dir>\")` is used to save the index to disk.\n   - Again, the specific directory name `<persist_dir>` is a placeholder, suggesting that users can specify a directory. The default directory, as mentioned earlier, is `./storage`.\n\nThus, in the LlamaIndex starter example, the call that saves an index to disk is `storage_context.persist()`, and the default directory name it uses, if none is specified, is `./storage`.",
